---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: ""
description: "A passion project to democratize publishing. Project Broadsheet is a full newsroom — editorial sections, reviews, a library, reader tools, search, and SEO — free to fork and keep."
permalink: /index.html
---
<section class="hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hero__inner">
      <div>
        <span class="hero__eyebrow">v{{ meta.version }} · MIT · A passion project</span>
        <h1 class="hero__title">{{ meta.tagline }}</h1>
        <p class="hero__subhead">{{ meta.subhead }}</p>
        <div class="hero__actions btn-group btn-group--balanced">
          <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/get-started/">Fork it and start</a>
          <a class="btn btn--outline btn--lg" href="/about/">Read the story</a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__meta">
          <span class="hero__meta-item">Nine editorial sections</span>
          <span class="hero__meta-item">27+ reader tools</span>
          <span class="hero__meta-item">Pagefind search</span>
          <span class="hero__meta-item">No subscriptions, ever</span>
        </div>
        <hr class="gold-rule hero__rule">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="social-strip">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="social-strip__inner">
      <span class="social-strip__item">In use at <strong><a href="{{ meta.liveExample }}">{{ meta.liveExampleName }}</a></strong></span>
      <span class="social-strip__item">Source on <strong><a href="{{ meta.github }}">GitHub</a></strong></span>
      <span class="social-strip__item"><strong>MIT</strong> licensed</span>
      <span class="social-strip__item">Built by <strong><a href="/about/">one person</a></strong></span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-features" id="home-features">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="home-features__header">
      <span class="eyebrow">What's included</span>
      <h2 class="home-features__title">A newsroom's worth of tools, packaged for one.</h2>
      <p class="home-features__summary">For a long time, the infrastructure that makes a publication feel like a publication — proper editorial sections, a reviews stack, a searchable archive, thoughtful reader tools — lived only inside major news organizations or behind SaaS paywalls. Project Broadsheet brings those tools out in the open.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="home-features__grid">
      {% for f in features.highlights %}
      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">{{ f.title }}</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">{{ f.summary }}</p>
        <ul class="feature-card__list">
          {% for point in f.points %}<li>{{ point }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: var(--space-xl);">
      <a class="btn btn--outline btn--lg" href="/features/">See every feature</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="home-features__header">
      <span class="eyebrow">Get started</span>
      <h2 class="home-features__title">Three commands to a live publication.</h2>
      <p class="home-features__summary">No sign-up, no account, no trial. Clone the repo, run a few commands, deploy wherever you want.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="how-it-works">
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step__num">1</div>
        <div>
          <div class="step__title">Fork</div>
          <p class="step__body">Clone <code>{{ meta.githubOwner }}/{{ meta.githubRepo }}</code>. Rename the folder. Make it yours.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step__num">2</div>
        <div>
          <div class="step__title">Configure</div>
          <p class="step__body">Edit <code>site.json</code> for metadata and sections. Edit <code>tokens.css</code> for colors and fonts. One file each.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step__num">3</div>
        <div>
          <div class="step__title">Publish</div>
          <p class="step__body">Push to GitHub. Cloudflare Pages, Netlify, or Vercel will deploy in under a minute.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="comparison-teaser">
      <span class="eyebrow">Why this exists</span>
      <p class="comparison-teaser__kicker">Because <strong>publishing shouldn't be rented</strong>, and because the tools big publications use shouldn't stay locked inside them.</p>
      <p style="color: var(--text-soft); max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 auto var(--space-lg); line-height: 1.6;">Substack takes 10% of your revenue. Ghost charges $9 to $199 a month for features. WordPress is its own whole ordeal. Those are fine options — they just aren't the only options. Project Broadsheet is what I wanted to use instead.</p>
      <a class="btn btn--outline btn--lg" href="/compare/">See the full comparison</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="home-features__header">
      <span class="eyebrow">In the wild</span>
      <h2 class="home-features__title">Publications running on Project Broadsheet</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="grid grid-2" style="max-width: 44rem; margin-inline: auto;">
      {% for s in showcase %}
      <a class="showcase-card" href="{{ s.url }}">
        <div class="showcase-card__image">{{ s.name }}</div>
        <div class="showcase-card__body">
          <div class="card__title">{{ s.name }}</div>
          <p class="card__summary">{{ s.summary }}</p>
          <div class="showcase-card__tags">
            {% for t in s.tags %}<span class="badge">{{ t }}</span>{% endfor %}
          </div>
        </div>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: var(--space-xl);">
      <a class="btn btn--outline" href="/showcase/">See showcase</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pricing-teaser section-sunken">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="pricing-teaser__title">Self-host it for free — or work with me directly.</h2>
    <p class="pricing-teaser__summary">Project Broadsheet is free to use forever. If you'd rather not spend a weekend on setup, I also offer hands-on help: setup, migration, custom work, and ongoing care. I'm selective about what I take on — I want to work on publications I'm proud to point at.</p>
    <div class="btn-group btn-group--balanced btn-group--center">
      <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/get-started/">Fork it and start</a>
      <a class="btn btn--outline btn--lg" href="/services/">Work with me</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
